;; expect: read-error bad_string
;; §8.4 slice 3.18 rule 3: a string literal is UTF-8 text in every position. A lone surrogate,
;; written by its escape, is refused by the elaborator — in a `def` as in a `fn` (a def's
;; refusal ends the reading): K reads a literal by decoding it, and only on valid bytes is the
;; encoding of the decoded text the bytes written. The erasure, which emits those bytes, keeps
;; the same check for itself
(import Init String)
(def d () String "a\u{D800}b")
(fn g () String "a\u{D800}b")
